cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use blood-panel-pipeline in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "blood-panel-pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/blood-panel-pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/blood-panel-pipeline"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A stdlib-only Python pipeline that turns raw laboratory panel exports into a
  queryable, provenance-tracked SQLite record. Four planes separate concerns:
  raw rows are kept verbatim and never rewritten, canonical rows are a parsed
  twin rebuilt on every run, deterministic rules decide what is mechanically
  true, and the model plane -- deliberately empty in this release -- may only
  explain, never decide. Unparsed cells are retained with a QC flag rather than
  dropped. Ships a 16-panel bilingual classifier, an A/B/C/D evidence-tier
  grading, and draft LOINC/UCUM seeds stamped unverified. Contains no
  measurements and no personal health data. Not medical advice and not a
  substitute for a clinician.
